    "standard": {
        "explanation": "<h3>The Building Blocks of Numbers</h3><p>Every number is built from smaller numbers called Factors.</p><h4>Key Concepts</h4><ul><li><strong>Factors:</strong> Numbers that divide exactly into another number (e.g., Factors of 12: 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 12).</li><li><strong>Multiples:</strong> Times tables of a number (e.g., Multiples of 5: 5, 10, 15, 20...).</li><li><strong>Prime Numbers:</strong> Numbers with only 2 factors: 1 and itself (2, 3, 5, 7, 11...).</li><li><strong>HCF (Highest Common Factor):</strong> The largest factor shared by two numbers.</li><li><strong>LCM (Lowest Common Multiple):</strong> The smallest multiple shared by two numbers.</li></ul><h4>Divisibility Rules (Shortcuts!)</h4><ul><li><strong>Divisible by 2:</strong> Ends in 0, 2, 4, 6, 8.</li><li><strong>Divisible by 3:</strong> Sum of digits is divisible by 3.</li><li><strong>Divisible by 5:</strong> Ends in 0 or 5.</li></ul>",
